# Wine ntdll conformance units that Windows itself does not pass on a runner, gated against a native run of the same
# binary instead of against 0 failures (tests/winetest/run_ntdll.cmake, header: PARITY; docs/slices/wt-ntdll-file.md).
#
#   <unit> <minimum number of assertions executed through the layer>
#
# A listed unit runs as on Windows (--platform=windows), must complete, execute at least the floor, and fail no
# assertion in two layer runs that the native run on the same runner passes. Add a unit here only with the failing
# lines of its native run recorded in its slice doc.
file 1300
# Diagnostic floors (docs/slices/wt-ntdll-rest.md), replaced by measured floors once each unit is measured.
# (exception is not here: the unit ends with an unhandled STATUS_DATATYPE_MISALIGNMENT natively on the runner too.)
info 1
pipe 1
sync 1
threadpool 2300
virtual 1
wow64 1
reg 500
